# =============================================================
# NextCRM Docker Environment Configuration
# =============================================================
#
# HOW TO USE THIS FILE
# --------------------
# 1. Copy it:        cp .env.docker .env
# 2. Edit it:        uncomment lines below and add your values
# 3. Start the app:  docker compose up -d
#
# Docker Compose automatically reads .env from this directory
# and injects the values into the app container. You do NOT
# need to edit Dockerfile or docker-compose.yml.
#
# WHAT YOU CAN SAFELY IGNORE
# --------------------------
# Internal services (Postgres, Inngest) already have
# working defaults baked into docker-compose.yml, and secrets are
# generated on first start. You only need to set values below to:
#   - Run it on a server (APP_URL, passwords)
#   - Enable an optional integration (OpenAI, Google OAuth, etc.)
#
# The app starts with NO .env file at all. Optional features
# stay disabled until you provide real keys.
#
# SECURITY
# --------
# .env is in .gitignore — your secrets stay local.
# Coolify/Portainer users: set these via the platform UI
# instead of a .env file. Same effect.
# =============================================================

# =============================================================
# REQUIRED: Initial admin account
# =============================================================
# This email becomes the admin user created by the seed script
# on first start. The app uses passwordless Email OTP to log in,
# so you MUST set this to a real email you control AND configure
# an email provider (RESEND_API_KEY below) so OTP codes can be
# delivered. Without an email provider, you can still read the
# OTP from the database directly while testing.
#
# Only used on first run (when no users exist in the database).
# Changing it later has no effect — create new admins from the
# Admin panel instead.
# =============================================================
ADMIN_EMAIL=you@example.com

# =============================================================
# REQUIRED FOR PRODUCTION: Internal service credentials
# =============================================================
# The bundled Postgres container defaults to the
# placeholder password "changeme". This is fine for local
# experimentation: Postgres is not exposed to the host. Set strong values before running this
# anywhere accessible (Coolify, VPS, production server). The
# same env var is used by both the service and the app, so a
# single override changes both sides.
# =============================================================
POSTGRES_USER=nextcrm
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=changeme
POSTGRES_DB=nextcrm


# --- Public URLs ---
# The URL people use to open NextCRM. Default is for a local test on this machine.
# APP_URL=https://crm.example.com

# --- Secrets ---
# Generated on first start and kept in the app_data volume, so they survive
# restarts and upgrades. Set them here instead if you prefer to manage them
# yourself (then back up this file). Never change them later: a new
# BETTER_AUTH_SECRET logs everyone out, a new EMAIL_ENCRYPTION_KEY makes
# stored mailbox passwords and API keys unreadable.
# BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=       # openssl rand -base64 32
# EMAIL_ENCRYPTION_KEY=     # openssl rand -hex 32
# Shared by the app and the bundled Inngest server (hex strings).
# INNGEST_SIGNING_KEY=      # openssl rand -hex 32
# INNGEST_EVENT_KEY=        # openssl rand -hex 16

# --- File storage (UploadThing) ---
# Create an app at https://uploadthing.com/dashboard and copy its token
# (API Keys > V7). Required for document and avatar uploads.
UPLOADTHING_TOKEN=

# --- Email ---
# Login codes are sent through Resend, so set RESEND_API_KEY (here or in
# Admin > Resend) and EMAIL_FROM (a sender verified in Resend). Without it,
# read the OTP from the database while testing.
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_...
# EMAIL_FROM=noreply@yourdomain.com
# RESEND_FROM_EMAIL=noreply@yourdomain.com   # campaigns and notifications
# RESEND_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# --- SMTP (optional, port 465 TLS, used by lib/sendmail.ts) ---
# EMAIL_HOST=smtp.example.com
# EMAIL_USERNAME=your-user
# EMAIL_PASSWORD=your-password

# --- AI (optional). Leave empty to use keys saved in the admin panel. ---
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_API_KEY=          # also required for embeddings / semantic search
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# AI_PROVIDER_ORDER=        # default OPENAI,GEMINI,OPENROUTER,ANTHROPIC
# OUTREACH_PER_MINUTE=      # AI outreach messages per minute in bulk (default 5)
# <PROVIDER>_MODELS[_LIGHT|_THINKING]=model-a,model-b   # per-tier fallback lists

# --- Google OAuth login (optional) ---
# GOOGLE_ID=your-google-client-id
# GOOGLE_SECRET=your-google-client-secret

# --- Google Calendar sync (optional) ---
# GOOGLE_CALENDAR_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_CALENDAR_CLIENT_SECRET=

# --- Firecrawl (optional, for contact enrichment) ---
# FIRECRAWL_API_KEY=fc-...

# --- E2B (optional, for agent enrichment) ---
# E2B_API_KEY=e2b_...

# --- Public lead/contact intake API token (optional) ---
# NEXTCRM_TOKEN=            # openssl rand -base64 32

# --- Advanced ---
# SEED_DEMO_DATA=1                      # demo CRM data on first start
# MAIL_ALLOW_PRIVATE_HOSTS=true         # mail servers on private IPs
# PLUGIN_HTTP_ALLOW_PRIVATE_HOSTS=true  # plugin HTTP calls to private IPs
